  partName: Left Front Bolt (2)
  description: The Left Front Bolt (2) is a tiny, complex-shaped component located
    at the top-left-center of the engine, made of Material.001, which plays a crucial
    role in securing the engine's front section, ensuring stability and preventing
    damage from vibrations, and its complex shape allows for a secure fit with adjacent
    parts. Its small size belies its importance in maintaining engine integrity.
    The bolt's position at the front of the engine also makes it prone to exposure
    to external factors, such as temperature fluctuations.
